WEBVTT

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.510
Look, the sky up above has begun to move.
Hora miageta sora ugokidashita yo

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.740
Your astonishment was so dazzling.
Odoroku kimi mabushikute

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.800
Should I forgive the lies you told me yesterday
Kinou tsuita uso mo yurusou kana

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.110
just because the morning light is so pretty?
Kesa no hikari kirei dakara

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:38.160
The sound of your laughter is always important to me
Kimi no warai goe itsu datte daiji da yo

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.810
because it gives me courage.
Yuuki kureru kara saa

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.750
It's not a lie.
Uso ja nai

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.450
It's a beauty really
It's a beauty really

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.600
Your voice whenever.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.100
It makes me have.
Your voice whenever.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:50.980
It makes me have.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:51.650
Even the silliest things sound dear,
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:57.970
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo
Even the silliest things sound dear,

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:01.530
if it's your voice I hear.
kimi no koe nara

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.800
You're sad whenever.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.110
It takes you back.
You're sad whenever.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:05.450
It takes you back.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:08.830
My heart runneth over.
Hamidasu kokoro

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:16.030
Unable to control myself, I set off at a run.
Osaerarenakute hashiri dashita yo

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.040
I can forever.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.280
What are you doing, Komiyama?

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.360
Do you have to ask?
It's almost Valentine's Day.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.830
I see, Valentine's Day...

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:50.540
The season when all the guys start cleaning out their lockers and desks.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:53.970
All in the pointless hope that
chocolate will be placed in them.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.370
Shut up. You won't know if it's
pointless or not until you try.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.510
Valentine's Chance Encounter

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.100
Thank you very much!

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.260
I'm glad they had some left.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.400
That's great, isn't it?

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:20.600
How many stores did we try, again?

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.970
It's because you helped me look for it.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.530
Thank you!

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.650
Stop it...

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.780
Getting embarrassed again...

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.630
I am not.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:31.890
You know...

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.590
Toujou, are you going shopping too?

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:41.820
Y-Yes. What about you
and Kitaouji-san?

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:43.610
Satsuki wanted to go shopping--

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.880
It's a date.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.140
We're going on a date, right?

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.690
Manaka, thank you for the present.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.150
W-What are you saying, Satsuki?!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:00.030
Well, I'll see you tomorrow, Manaka. It's been fun.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.820
W-Wait, Satsuki!

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.690
It wasn't a date at all.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:08.320
Satsuki dragged me along on a shopping trip.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:13.270
I'm going to go after Satsuki right now,
but please believe me.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:24.210
Satsuki!

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:28.270
Yo. Thanks for chasing after me.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.360
Thanks for nothing!

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.340
Why did you lie about
us being on a date?

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.350
I saw a chance.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:36.850
A chance?

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:40.350
A chance for me to tear your
relationship with Toujou-san apart.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.600
B-But, a lie like that...

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:46.510
Just what do you like
about her, anyway?

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:50.340
You can talk about silly stuff with me,

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:53.040
and I think we always
have fun together.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.810
I get it.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.620
I think so too.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.600
Amazing.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:09.590
I've never felt such a powerful embrace.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.060
I hate you.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:15.630
Why won't you hug me back?

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.760
You told me that you like me,

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.530
so why won't you only look at me?

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.240
I can't take this anymore.
I'm tired of it!

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.530
Even though I'm being so forward with you...

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:32.910
You're an idiot! I hate you so much!

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:34.400
Satsuki.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.620
But in reality, I hate myself the most.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:41.630
Sa-Satsuki!

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:49.170
This is... the same thing that
happened with Nishino.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.090
Because I'm a loser. Because I can't decide which girl I like.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:57.190
I get what I deserve.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:00.530
But it seems like returning
Satsuki's embrace

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:03.390
would have hurt her
a lot more in the end.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:10.350
I'm so stupid! Why'd I have to go and say those things?

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:29.030
Good morning, Manaka-kun.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.150
Ah, good morning, Toujou.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.280
I fail. She really hates me.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:53.160
What, he can't spare a
"good morning" for me?

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.320
Fine, I won't talk to him either.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:05:59.530
Sorry!

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.050
I forgot my math book today.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.410
Can I look off yours?

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:08.240
Doesn't your boyfriend over there
usually lend you his?

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.320
M-My boyfriend? Who's that?

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:11.960
Please, just this once?

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:16.920
How come I can't just be honest?

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:22.360
In the end, several days passed without
us being able to fix our relationship.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:26.030
And when Valentine's Day
rolled around...

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.270
I'm off.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:31.900
Junpei, you'd better get chocolate
from at least one girl this year.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.190
Lay off me!

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.950
Is after school today okay?

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.120
Of course it's okay.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.700
It's out of duty.
Don't misunderstand.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.370
Chocolate...

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:47.530
Thank you.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:49.220
Okay, sure, thank you.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.460
There's nothing inside...

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:04.670
No surprises here.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:06.700
I guess it's hopeless.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:10.780
My shoe box was my last chance,
and it came up empty.

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:15.610
For guys who aren't popular,
Valentine's Day is just another day.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.770
I thought Satsuki would give me some.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:26.090
I thought I'd somehow be able to
make up with her on Valentine's Day.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:35.880
Ah, umm...

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.210
T-Toujou.

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:42.720
M-Manaka-kun, if you'd like, could you please take this?

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.070
Or maybe... you can't?

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.820
Oh, believe me, I certainly can!

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:56.640
Thank you. This is the first time I've ever gotten chocolate.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.420
What am I <i>saying?</i>

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.610
I really thought it might trouble you.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:07.230
But I heard about
Nishino-san from Yui-chan.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:10.300
And I thought it might be okay to...

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.390
But this is different.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:17.260
It's like... a feeling of gratitude.

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.290
Gratitude?

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:23.620
It feels like the world's
opened up for me

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:26.070
ever since I got to know you.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:30.900
You read my novel. And I was
able to try scriptwriting, too.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.900
I was also able to befriend the types of people I'd never talked to before.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:37.400
Like Komiyama-kun and Sotomura-kun...

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.480
Given the way she's smiling...

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:42.210
She may as well have told me she likes me.

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:43.580
Me too.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:47.660
Because of you, the world opened up for me as well.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.160
Manaka-kun...

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:58.670
What a fool I am. This is my first attempt at making chocolates...

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.200
I did the best I could, but...

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:04.930
Well, whatever. It's a
sticky failure of a chocolate.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:41.830
Chocolates? For me? Who from?

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:45.710
Could they be from Satsuki?

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:49.280
She couldn't give it to me directly because of our fight...

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:53.010
Seriously, that girl is so
dishonest with herself!

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.220
I'm home!

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:59.060
Eh?! Junpei, what's that?! Congratulations!

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:06.920
Yo, Junpei.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:09.310
Oh, Yui. What is it?

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:13.580
You're back this soon after that teary separation?

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:16.580
I'm here for the Oumi Academy entrance exams.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.080
According to the news,
this year's exam is 4.8 times harder.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:22.880
Tough barrier, isn't it?

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:26.600
Is that really something to say to an exam candidate?

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:27.800
Hmm?

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:30.760
Ah! Chocolate!

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:33.440
Wow, you even got two of them.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.340
Well, yeah.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.470
From Toujou-san and Satsuki-chan?

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:41.350
Then it's only obligatory chocolate.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.620
How so?

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:46.040
Wait, isn't that round one homemade?

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:50.530
Homemade? I see... it's homemade.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:54.620
Even after we fought, Satsuki
took the trouble to make it by hand.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:56.270
What a nice girl.

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:00.150
All right, it's tasting time!

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:04.410
Why are <i>you</i> eating them first?!

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:06.630
It's just one measly chocolate!

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:09.230
That's not the point!

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:12.160
It's Valentine's, Valentine's!

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:12.640
Give it!

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:14.940
I already ate it.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:18.030
It was good. Another one, please!

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.450
No! The rest are all mine.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:31.570
I never knew Valentine's
chocolate could be this good.

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:33.250
I'm glad to be alive.

00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:42.010
Junpei's nose is bleeding!

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.380
Mrs. Manaka! Tissue! Tissue!

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:45.890
How pathetic!

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:49.830
Not even kindergartners get nosebleeds from eating chocolate these days!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.270
I suppose I didn't have to
throw it away.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.040
I should have just given them to him.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.260
Stupid me.

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:18.360
At this rate, I won't have the chance to apologize to Manaka.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:20.470
Manaka.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:23.930
Hey. Erm... that is...

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:26.430
Thank you for the chocolates.

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:29.110
I was happy.

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:31.670
Are you serious? I mean, that chocolate was--!

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:35.400
Manaka... You picked them up?

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:40.930
I picked them up and then I ate them.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:47.300
No way. You actually
<i>found</i> those things?

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:50.330
Well, of course I found them.

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:51.890
But...

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.770
They really sucked, didn't they?

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:58.770
That was the first time I've ever made sweets from scratch.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:03.810
I know my personality and those kinds of stunts don't really mix.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:06.760
No, that's not true at all.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:10.650
At first, I thought they were store-bought chocolates.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:12.410
The taste was on the bitter side.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:15.180
Those were dark chocolates, right? I liked them.

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:19.210
Store-bought chocolates?

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.140
That's right...

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.560
I did put some effort
into wrapping them.

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:26.380
Did they turn out bitter
because I over-baked them?

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:27.810
But...

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.820
Manaka... you're so kind!

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:36.750
You and that facial expression don't mix, you dummy.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:39.410
Those chocolates you made by hand for me...

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:42.630
...really made me happy.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:49.170
Yes, yes, that's much more like you.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:51.260
Manaka, you kidder!

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:53.770
Hey, let go!

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:55.320
I won't let go~!

00:13:55.320 --> 00:14:00.300
Sweet Painful Chocolate

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:03.850
Thank goodness.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.250
I was able to make up with Satsuki.

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:10.770
Manaka-kun!

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:16.020
I wrote more of my novel.
Would you like to read it?

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:21.570
Of course! That last part really left me hanging.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:25.310
Let's meet after school in the Film Club room.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:27.580
Ah... roger that.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:32.920
Satsuki... and Toujou...

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:35.580
Because of Valentine's Day,

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:39.720
I feel like my relationships with
them are going to change.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:49.460
Did I get lost or something?

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:55.190
I probably shouldn't have explored the school all alone after the exams finished.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.340
No, this isn't the right way.

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:02.640
What should I do?
Go back to the school again?

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:11.010
It's impossible.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:14.660
I don't remember the
corners I turned at.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:17.450
What's wrong?

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:21.200
Yui-chan, right?

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.390
I'm guessing... you're lost?

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:28.900
Let's see, you were Junpei's friend...

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.570
Nishino. Nishino Tsukasa.

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:35.090
That's right, you're Nishino-san!

00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:37.940
I'm so glad I ran into someone I know.

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:44.000
Oh yeah, you go to
Oumi Academy, don't you?

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:47.490
So if I'm accepted,
I'll be a grade below you.

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:50.000
That's right. I hope you get in.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:53.080
Me too! I studied really hard over winter break--

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:56.790
I'll be all right from here.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:59.270
Junpei's house is pretty nearby.

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:02.200
Is Junpei-kun doing well?

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:03.490
He's well.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:06.510
Oh yeah, get a load of this!

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:11.020
After he ate some hand-made Valentine's chocolates,

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:13.490
he suddenly got a nosebleed!

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:16.210
Pretty childish for a
high school boy, I'd say.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:19.280
Huh? What's wrong?

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:24.530
So, he really wolfed
those chocolates down.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.190
Thank you, Junpei-kun!

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:30.390
Anyway... here, right?

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:32.820
Hopefully I'll see you
at school this spring.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.480
Bye-bye, Yui-chan!

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.730
I wonder why Nishino-san said "thank you."

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:45.710
Weren't those chocolates from Satsuki-chan? How strange.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.400
It's almost as if <i>she</i> made them.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:50.610
It can't be!

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.480
Maybe those chocolates were actually from...

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:55.350
Yui-chan?

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.360
Mrs. Manaka!

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.520
How was the test?

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:00.750
No problems!

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:02.760
Ah, good for you!

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:05.990
I thought I'd make stew for dinner, just for you.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:07.750
Eh? Stew?

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:12.000
Yui would REAAALLY love to have oysters in it!

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.530
How convenient!

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:18.000
I just received a ton of oysters from your house today.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.000
Yahoo! Yay!

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:24.740
Huh? I get the feeling I just had something on my mind, but...

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:26.690
Well, whatever.

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:36.120
Was it bad?

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:39.570
No... It was great!

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:44.870
But I'm curious about which of the two heroines the protagonist will choose.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:46.100
Right.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.860
The beautiful princess that helps put the protagonist on the proper path,

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:52.880
or the weaver girl that has the same dreams as him.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:55.820
I wonder which one he'll choose...

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:56.820
Well...

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.880
N-No, I don't want to hear it right now.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.850
Good, because I still haven't decided it.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:03.410
I see.

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:05.790
I'll be anticipating the next part, then.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.340
Isn't it about time to head home?

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:13.890
Erm... can't we keep
talking a bit longer?

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:15.890
Talking? About what?

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.340
Anything's okay.

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:21.990
For example, you know... that.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.140
We finally were able
to be alone together.

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:28.020
She gave me chocolate,
and we've gotten even closer.

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.660
You know...

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:33.240
It seems like there's
an interesting movie

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:35.290
coming out during spring break.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:37.350
What kind of movie?

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:38.870
It's fantasy.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:50.650
Manaka-kun?

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:57.270
Manaka... kun.

00:18:57.930 --> 00:19:01.850
Toujou told me her chocolates were meant to express gratitude, but...

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:04.270
...I can't help thinking
there was more to them.

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:06.580
Of course, I have
feelings for Satsuki, too.

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:10.790
But if Toujou confessed to me,

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:13.230
I wouldn't hesitate anymore.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.640
I won't get a good
answer if I rush things.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.460
Yet I'm rushing anyway.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:26.810
A girl's wrist is this weak...

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:30.100
If I held it any tighter,
would it break?

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:33.060
If I were to embrace Toujou tightly...

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:37.750
Would the relationship we've built so far also break?

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:48.740
M-Manaka-kun...?

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:53.030
But I wanted to embrace her.

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:55.430
Definitely...

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:57.800
Ever since that time...

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:12.890
S-Shall we go home?

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:14.070
Sure.

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:28.150
Manaka-kun.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.560
I think I know which
of the two heroines

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:36.040
the protagonist in my novel would choose.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:38.780
I feel like I just now figured it out.

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:43.170
I'll see you tomorrow, Manaka-kun.

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:44.260
Yeah.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:47.420
Toujou.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:53.990
I didn't tell her I liked her,
nor did she tell me she liked me.

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:55.450
Exactly one year ago...

00:20:56.220 --> 00:20:58.900
I fell in love with the figure I saw on the rooftop...

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:01.690
...and I feel like I've finally conveyed that feeling.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:05.440
I'm... so happy I could almost die.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:13.650
Hey! Quit wandering around in the street! You got a death wish?!

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:17.660
I'm sorry! I don't want to die yet!

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:31.400
Junpei, what are you smiling about?

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:32.560
You're creeping me out.

00:21:47.690 --> 00:21:49.030
Go go!
Ike ike

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:05.400
Enchant me, love is courage and charm.
Misete koi wa dokyou ni aikyou

00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:08.510
